From ec29b4373c36db5655499012908f130e326526d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NEXUS <nexus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:44:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] nexus_engine: game window hidden until its first frame,
 real loading progress, NEXUS Home key

- The game window was created visible before the game loaded. While the engine
  thread loaded the game (and its shader cache) the window received no
  messages, so Windows showed an unpainted black window with a white frame over
  the NEXUS loading screen. It is now created hidden and shown (fullscreen,
  raised) with the first presented frame, or after 20 s if nothing is shown.
- Disk shader cache loading reports its real progress (loadStage/loadDone/
  loadTotal in the status) for the NEXUS loading screen.
- NEXUS Home: request "homeKey" (an SDL key name, "" for none) and
  "homeButton" (controller Guide/Home). The key is taken by NEXUS only when no
  player-1 control is bound to it; otherwise it goes to the game and the status
  reports homeKeyConflict. Each press counts in homePresses.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X7yw1ZJY9GYi2KYHfiXxvY
